                <pb facs="0917" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg797"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Lithuania/93: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Lithuania (Stafford) to the Secretary of
                        State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kaunas</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-12-13T16:00:00+01:00">December 13,
                            1932—4 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received December 13—11:55 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>22. Minister for Foreign Affairs informs me despite request for revision or
                    postponement preparations for payment of interest due on the 15 being made.
                    Whether payment will be unconditional will depend upon action of other debtors
                    particularly France.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stafford</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
